From d146b1513b5848afb8a5e41420a85d477d44d4c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:54:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Mark wake-episode freshness only for local triage
 cards

d02605e skipped the first probe-less park's evidence for ANY locally created
card. A runnable card can reach a peer and be parked on a probe P there before
this home's first park; that park then carried no reset and the undelivered
foreign episode kept its age/count after delayed sync.

Freshness is now set only by the local 'created' event of a triage card (not
runnable, so no peer can have parked it first) and dropped by any status
transition except a direct triage -> scheduled park (including raw/synced
remote transitions, via a status trigger), by a probe park, and by the first
probe-less park. Runnable created cards are never fresh.

test_never_probed_park_adds_no_evidence and the 'fresh entry'/'fresh local
creation' first-park assertions (added by this PR, not original acceptance)
encoded the unsafe skip for runnable cards; they now expect the reset.
Triage-park atomic cardinality (test_kanban_triage_park.py, six cases: direct
triage -> scheduled appends one event) is unchanged.

Proof: test_kanban_wake_episode_probeless.py on d02605 prod code: 13 FAILED,
7 passed (new RED: created card -> foreign undelivered P -> first home no-probe
park [scheduled, continued], plus no-status-write continued, triage exits, probe
park); GREEN here 20/20. Broad wake episode/check/triage/sync/create set: 65
files, 858 passed, 0 failed (retries 0). Mutations: 7/7 killed
(mut-triage-fresh.log).
